   "quotes": {
    "confounding": "In an attempt to minimize confounding, propensity score matching techniques were also used to match patients to make treated and untreated individuals more comparable.",
    "selection": "This retrospective, observational study included US military, NATO military, host military/police, and local civilian patients who were injured in combat operations in Afghanistan in the 3-year, 6-month period from October 1, 2010, to March 31, 2014.",
    "classification": "Prehospital and hospital treatment records were reviewed to determine whether or not each patient was administered TXA",
    "deviations": "Furthermore, follow-up time was adjusted to account for immortal time/survival bias by calculating person time for the TXA group from the time of TXA administration rather than time of injury.",
    "missingData": "There were seven cases that had missing values, which were excluded from subsequent multivariate analyses. Sensitivity analysis showed that inclusion of these cases with either imputed values or with missing indicators did not change the results.",
    "measurement": "Subsequent review of medical records for all patients in this study diagnosed with a PE indicated that only two patients actually died with a PE, and detailed chart review in both cases concluded that PE was incidental",
    "reporting": "All proportional hazards models were estimated with cluster-adjusted, robust standard error estimates to account for nonindependence of observations"
   }
